ed study correction adds orientation in the direction of increasing t, making e the unique valid displayed choice. All original DOM, screenshots, solver decisions, grades, choices, field and answer identities remain retained."} {"question" "q-22301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the straight line given by the following parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+3t \\\\ y=2-4t \\\\ z=2+t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind a vector that is parallel to the line." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aef1fad50ee8c569cbfa51288a76516d58d4b185ea82ae78cbdc5a034a77741" "basis" 1538 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-22301" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's find the corresponding vector equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1+3t \\\\ 2-4t \\\\ 2+t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ -4t \\\\ t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nThis implies that the line passes through the point $(1,2,2)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041770/state.json" "file_sha256" "2aef1fad50ee8c569cbfa51288a76516d58d4b185ea82ae78cbdc5a034a77741" "basis" 