me/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=5+t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1147e6467084d36ef9c60403f071a25a09c5e10214e4959d78fc7a7593667836" "basis" 2295 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-36026" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=4t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1147e6467084d36ef9c60403f071a25a09c5e10214e4959d78fc7a7593667836" "basis" 2295 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Fill in the missing parts in the parametric equations below that describe all the points on the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ},$ where $P(-5,7,1)$ and $Q(-4,-1,6).$\n\n| $x=$ | {{field-1}} | $t\\in [$ {{field-2}} $,1]$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $y=$ | $7-8t$ |  |\n| $z=$ | $1+5t$ |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1147e6467084d36ef9c60403f071a25a09c5e10214e4959d78fc7a7593667836" "basis" 2295 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the line passing through the given points. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ -8t \\\\ 5t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5+t \\\\ 7-8t \\\\ 1+5t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ \n\nTo get the equations for the line segment, we take only $t\\in [0,1].$ Notice that substitution of $t=0$ in the above equation gives the coordinates of $P$ and substitution of $t=1$ gives the coordinates of $Q.$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the line segment $\\overset{―}{PQ}$ are the following:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-5+t \\\\ y=7-8t \\\\ z=1+5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\,t\\in [0,1]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/state.json" "file_sha256" "1147e6467084d36ef9c60403f071a25a09c5e10214e4959d78fc7a7593667836" "basis" 2295 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14068356/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-236986" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/line