cademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-70716" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b16ddaac7c6a0f615f35b49c381df7fb4526c819aeb36121b03237aeaca04"} {"question" "q-70716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-70716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-70716" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-22318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/assets/58076d96d149ff4521103fd15c7187bc1a58595ab20f28be92be0f79385aee61.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-22318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,1,4)$ and $Q(3,-2,2).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$,  as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4t \\\\ -3t \\\\ -2t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+4t \\\\ 1-3t \\\\ 4-2t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Therefore, the parametric equations are:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+4t \\\\ y=1-3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-22318" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b16ddaac7c6a0f615f35b49c381df7fb4526c819aeb36121b03237aeaca04"} {"question" "q-22318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-22318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+4t \\\\ y=1-3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=-t \\\\ y=t \\\\ z=4t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=3-t \\\\ y=-2+t \\\\ z=2+4t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=4-t \\\\ y=-3+t \\\\ z=-2+4t\\end{aligned}"] ["math" "{\\begin{aligned}x=4t \\\\ y=-3t \\\\ z=-2t\\end{aligned}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-22318" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+4t \\\\ y=1-3t \\\\ z=4-2t\\end{aligned}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-32817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/assets/1ffc0945ea74b1bd467a0b9935ee28b88be004c18b11492d67ecdfec56e1bb09.png)\n\nFind the parametric equations of the line shown in the figure above." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-32817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,3,2)$ and $Q(2,4,5).$ Now, we need to find a direction vector that is parallel to the given line. We can use the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ} \\\\  & =\\overset{\\to }{OQ}-\\overset{\\to }{OP} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the vector equation of the line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =p+tv \\\\ r & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+t[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3t \\\\ t \\\\ 3t\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1+3t \\\\ 3+t \\\\ 2+3t\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ And finally, the parametric equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1+3t \\\\ y=3+t \\\\ z=2+3t\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-32817" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4d7b16ddaac7c6a0f615f35b49c381df7fb4526c819aeb36121b03237aeaca04"} {"question" "q-32817" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14083350/state.json" "file_sha256" "8699f9215a70017c858b7baf13de3401e0afd6f3ccd047721dec71d3ce6c7fcf"} {"question" "q-32817" "field" "selection" "attribu